defineOwnT -- SEQ 457 R0 (Tony, 2026-10-29): defineCapture Shape A's certificate, pre-registered on trunk.

Shape A: in aCTionTraiT, under NewGroup only, a definition's own name that resolved outside the current registry and arrives
WITH A VALUE gets a fresh node, and the value is written there. A bare name keeps its reference; attribute traits keep writing
through. Recon: docs/objectModelRecon.md section 27.

  DO-1  Grokking's counter (bootstrap digit set, data 3) -- today unitTests' counter=0 writes into it (data 5)
  DO-2  UnitTests' counter -- its own 0, a count (data 5), on both
  DO-3/4  cOMMANDs stop / compile -- today they carry DesignDocs' prose (data 13); intended no data (0)
  DO-5/6  DesignDocs' stop / compile entries keep their prose, on both
  DO-7/8  KantGrammar's LOOPRESTRICt loopOnAttributes / loopOnMembers -- same value as Grokking's on both; today the SAME BODY
          (the define wrote into Grokking's), intended their own body
  DO-9  KantGrammar's ANYORNUm member NumbeR is a bare reference to Grokking's NumbeR -- the same body on both
  DO-10 GroupFields' taG accessor -- today DoTagT's taG="ENCLOSING" writes into it (cursorReadTb's shape); intended no data
  DO-11 DoTagT's own taG reads ENCLOSING (a lookup by subscript, not the accessor), on both

Rows read values and data kinds by value, and identity by addrOf's BODY column (H13: "is this the same thing, reached through
another face" is a body question). The taG define comes last because a registry field named taG shadows the accessor for that
registry's own reads (recon 19f).
